Why Is Demand Increasing
Growth of Biologics and Specialty Medicines: Increasing production and distribution of biologics, vaccines, cell and gene therapies, and specialty pharmaceuticals is creating greater demand for specialized logistics infrastructure.
Temperature-Controlled Distribution: Pharmaceutical products often require precise storage and transportation conditions, driving investment in cold-chain facilities, validated packaging, monitoring systems, and specialized vehicles.
Supply Chain Visibility: Real-time tracking, digital documentation, IoT monitoring, and automated logistics management are improving visibility and helping pharmaceutical companies maintain product integrity throughout distribution.

Pharmaceutical Logistics Watch: Cold Chain and Advanced Monitoring
Cold-chain logistics is becoming increasingly important as pharmaceutical portfolios shift toward temperature-sensitive products. Logistics providers are expanding refrigerated warehousing, specialized transportation, packaging and validation capabilities, while digital monitoring technologies are helping track temperature, location, and shipment conditions throughout the supply chain.

